+// A ring of what the renderer did to guest memory, for the launches that die on a corrupted guest heap.
+//
+// The renderer writes into the guest's memory itself (labels, readbacks, register tables), tells the GPU to
+// write there, and with shared buffers lets the GPU use guest memory as it is.  When a guest thread faults on a
+// wild pointer or aborts, the last million of those events are written to kyty-write-journal-<pid>-<n>.bin in
+// the current directory (fps120/journal.py reads it), so that the bytes the guest tripped over can be matched
+// to the renderer write that put them there, if one did.  KYTY_WRITE_JOURNAL=0 turns it off.
+
